    Given a returning customer in the Bronze tier
    When a basket subtotal of 10000 cents is priced
    Then the customer is charged 9500 cents

  @happy-path
  Scenario: Returning customer in the Silver tier is charged the Silver price
    Given a returning customer in the Silver tier
    When a basket subtotal of 10000 cents is priced
    Then the customer is charged 9000 cents

  @happy-path
  Scenario: Returning customer in the Gold tier is charged the Gold price
    Given a returning customer in the Gold tier
    When a basket subtotal of 10000 cents is priced
    Then the customer is charged 8500 cents

  @edge-case
  Scenario: Returning customer in the Bronze tier on a very small basket has the reduction land on a whole cent
    Given a returning customer in the Bronze tier
    When a basket subtotal of 7 cents is priced
    Then the customer is charged 7 cents

  # Open decisions (escalated to DISCUSS, no scenario written):
  # 1. Platinum tier: reduction not agreed, no expected value exists.
  # 2. Rounding direction: AC-4 is titled "in the customer's favour" yet expects 7 cents charged
  #    on a 7 cent subtotal (no reduction applied). Only the 7 -> 7 example is settled; the
  #    rounding rule for any other subtotal is not.
EOF
